    "header": {
      "primary_content": [
        {
          "text": "When you start planning your trip to Thailand, one of the first questions you may have is, ‘when is the best time to visit?’ Although any month can be a good month to visit Thailand, the answer will depend on what is most important to you for your holiday. If maximising your budget is at the top of your list, consider visiting Thailand during the low season months from May to September. Internal flights and accommodation are often discounted during this time making a holiday in Thailand even better value for money than usual. If you are looking to explore the Thai countryside, October to January can be ideal with cooler temperatures and the scenery at its most picturesque. And if you are seeking a relaxing beach holiday, December to April tends to be the most popular period.",
          "url": null,
          "urls": null
        },
        {
          "text": "There are regional variations in the weather, but broadly speaking there are three seasons in Thailand; cool season, hot season, and the green season (also known as the rainy season).",
          "url": null,
          "urls": null
        }
      ],
